## 3. Target Audience & Searcher Profile

The primary searcher is a **renter at the active decision stage**: someone who has already started searching for apartments, knows they want to reduce upfront costs, and is looking for either specific listings with specials or a strategy to find them. This includes first-time renters managing tight move-in budgets, people relocating on short timelines, renters in high-supply markets with genuine negotiating leverage, and renters with credit or income challenges searching for low-barrier entry options (confirmed by PAA questions on no-credit-check and low-income specials).

They are in the **comparison-to-transaction** stage of the renter journey. They are not researching whether to rent; they are trying to reduce the financial friction of doing so. They expect either a list of current local specials (which brightplace cannot provide without location context) or a clear guide to finding specials on their own. The article must deliver the latter with enough specificity that it feels as useful as the former.

